<title>INDIA: India relaxes lending norms for exporting firms.</title>
<headline>India relaxes lending norms for exporting firms.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) on Tuesday said Indian exporters would be allowed to give trade-related advances to their importer clients out of their EEFC (exchange earners foreign currency account) funds.</p>
<p>It said in a letter to banks that these advances out of the EEFC account will not need prior approval, provided the advance does not exceed $3.0 million.</p>
<p>RBI said a separate communication would be sent to authorised dealers.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
